  "section_notes": "The final rules are strong on incident reporting and require 55°C testing with a 5% corrective-action threshold, but they do not automatically stop sales above 5%, which is a weakening for Northwind. Remote shut-off retrofit is set at six years with a feasible-alternative escape, fire suppression is built-in at 36 months, and S5 creates a mandatory recall process at 8 incidents/100k but lets the regulator decide remedies and possible resumption of sales."
